<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY TO OFFER 7YR BONDS OF HUF5BLN ON JULY 3.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY TO OFFER 7YR BONDS OF HUF5BLN ON JULY 3.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction five</p>
<p>billion forint worth of the seven-year government bonds of</p>
<p>2004/F series on July 3, the Government Debt Management Agency</p>
<p>(AKK) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    7 July, 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   24 March, 2004</p>
<p>    Day of auction	     3 July, 1997</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	   101.00 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (April 10)     101.67 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a floating interest, calculated</p>
<p>every half year, adding three percent to year-on-year consumer</p>
<p>inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on March 24. The</p>
<p>starting interest is 20.7 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
